{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ stress memory \"studies show\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_471524864#8_1021747916","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1200","rank":1,"snippet":"confusion and memory issues in older people. u000e Emotional issues Depression and anxiety have been linked to short-term memory issues. In most cases the effects are considered temporary and reversible if the depression or anxiety problem is resolved.u000e A condition called “pseudodementia” can occur in people following the onset of depression, along with dementia-like symptoms like forgetfulness and disorientation.u000e Other emotional situations can also reduce memory abilities, including grief, loneliness and traumatic events. Stress Stress has diverse effects on memory: it can heighten it under some conditions and impair normal <cover>memory function under others.u000e Some studies show that the stress </cover>hormone, cortisol, can be the source of problem with memory retrieval aside from the stress itself.u000e Injury Traumatic brain injury can wipe out memory both temporarily and permanently, depending on the natural and extensiveness of the damage. If forgetfulness is becoming an issue for you, learn more about the nutrients your brain needs for good memory function.\" , \"start_char\": 5441.000000 , \"title\": \"Factors That Can Impair Your Memory - Better Mind\" , \"url\": \"https://www.bettermind.com/articles/"}}
