{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_3299501977#7_3644839079","relevance":3,"reason":"This result directly summarizes studies on stress effects on memory via corticosterone, including that lower corticosterone fluctuations can prevent stress-related recognition-memory impairment, corticosterone can enhance formation or persistence of long-term memory depending on timing, and stress facilitates consolidation but disrupts reconsolidation of emotional memory.","learned":"Stress-hormone effects on memory depend strongly on timing, dose, and memory phase: stress may enhance consolidation/long-term formation but impair recognition or reconsolidation."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1211","reason":"The current query is yielding highly relevant direct evidence on stress effects on memory, so continue to the next result."}}
