{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_36044806#9_82271439","relevance":3,"reason":"This is from a review dedicated to stress effects on learning and memory and directly answers the question: stress effects depend on memory stage and timing; stress long before encoding impairs formation, stress shortly before/after learning generally enhances later memory, and stress before retrieval impairs recall.","learned":"Stress-memory effects are time- and stage-dependent: distant pre-encoding stress can impair formation, near-encoding/post-learning stress can enhance consolidation/performance, and pre-retrieval stress can impair recall."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1212","reason":"This query is retrieving direct grade-3 evidence from a dedicated review on stress effects across memory stages, so continue to find more relevant segments."}}
