{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_417391433#16_1008076675","relevance":1,"reason":"The snippet is from a stress-education page and its headings include 'Effects of stress on memory,' 'Stress hormones and memory,' and 'Stress, emotions and memory,' but the visible passage is mainly navigation/overview and does not yet provide evidence about what studies show.","learned":"Humanstress.ca may contain a dedicated section on stress hormones and memory, but the snippet alone does not show the findings."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_417391433#16_1008076675","reason":"The page appears to have a dedicated stress-and-memory section; inspecting the full document may reveal direct evidence suitable for grade 3."}}
{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_417391433#16_1008076675"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_417391433#16_1008076675","document":"Acute vs. chronic stress - CESH / CSHS ... Acute vs. chronic stress Acute vs. chronic stress Acute stress Chronic stress Close-up on… chronic stress Cardiovascular Function and Salt Cardiovascular Function and Water Cholesterol Insulin Resistance and Type II Diabetes Truncal Obesity  ... The end result is truncal obesity or fat around our midsection. The unfortunate thing is that our brain and stress response system do not know the difference and take for granted that we have used up the energy. Our brains have not changed much since we were hunter-gathers chasing mammoths, so we react similarly to the stressors of the modern world! These are but a few examples of how stress hormones are vital to our health. The take home message here is that our body and brain maintain their normal functioning ( homeostasis) through the delicate and precise interactions between many systems. The stress response system and its end product cortisol are key players in these interactions. When the cortisol system becomes deregulated, it affects all other systems that depend on its integrity to function. Stress WHAT IS STRESS? History of stress Biology of stress Stressors UNDERSTAND YOUR STRESS Recipe for stress Recognize your stress Acute vs. chronic stress Stages of chronic stress Types of chronic stress TRICK YOUR STRESS Principles of stress management Coping strategies Coping with stress – To keep in mind Coping with stress: Quick tricks Long-term stress management EFFECTS OF STRESS ON MEMORY Stress hormones and memory Stress, emotions and memory Is your memory affected by stress?","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
