{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_417391433#16_1008076675","relevance":1,"reason":"The full text available is primarily an acute-vs-chronic stress education page with navigation links to 'Effects of stress on memory' and related subtopics, but it does not include direct study findings about stress and memory.","learned":"Humanstress.ca likely has relevant stress-and-memory subpages, but this particular document fragment does not contain the evidence."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"stress hormones and memory\" cortisol)","reason":"Search directly for the likely dedicated subtopic 'Stress hormones and memory' with cortisol to find evidence on how stress hormones affect memory."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"stress hormones and memory\" cortisol)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1771132116#2_2670371492","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1223","rank":1,"snippet":"studied to make their discovery. Still, researchers say it’s important to remember that stress hormones represent only one factor when it comes to mental decline and memory loss as we age. For example, a study out of the University of California found that sleep deprivation is connected with brain degeneration and memory loss in older adults. When it comes to middle-aged men, another study found that those who drink more than two and a half drinks per day are likely to show signs of memory loss and cognitive decline up to six years sooner than men who are light drinkers or who don’t drink. Calling all HuffPost superfans! Sign up for membership to become a founding member and help shape HuffPost’s next chapter Join HuffPost BEFORE YOU GO PHOTO GALLERY 8 Guidelines For Stress-Free Aging MORE: Fifty Health Post50 Memory Loss Well Being <cover>Cortisol\" , \"start_char\": 1691.000000 , \"title\": \"Study Reveals Surprising Link Between Stress And Memory Loss | HuffPost\" , \"url\": \"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/2014/06/17/stress-hormones-and-memory-</cover>loss_n_5503444.html\" }"}}
