{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1569600860#3_3202837750","relevance":3,"reason":"This dedicated stress-and-memory article directly summarizes a meta-analysis of 113 stress studies: stress affects memory; stress before or during encoding can impede memory formation; stressor-related material may be remembered better; post-encoding stress can improve memory formation and retrieval; cortisol increases but is not simply proportional to impairment.","learned":"A meta-analysis of stress-memory studies found timing and relevance matter: stress before/during encoding may impair memory, stressor-related material may be enhanced, and post-encoding stress may improve memory formation/retrieval."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1226","reason":"The current query is yielding direct evidence from a dedicated stress-and-memory article, including meta-analysis findings; check the next result for additional relevant segments before switching queries."}}
